{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The key used to look up an entry in a strings file or strings dictionary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LocalizedStringKey"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializers for several SwiftUI types – such as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Toggle"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Picker"},{"type":"text","text":" and others –  implicitly look up a localized string when you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provide a string literal. When you use the initializer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text(\"Hello\")"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI creates a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for you and uses that to look up a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"localization of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hello"},{"type":"text","text":" string. This works because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conforms to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/ExpressibleByStringLiteral"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Types whose initializers take a ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedStringKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" usually have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a corresponding initializer that accepts a parameter that conforms to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/StringProtocol","type":"text"},{"text":". Passing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" variable to these initializers avoids localization, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually appropriate when the variable contains a user-provided value.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As a general rule, use a string literal argument when you want","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"localization, and a string variable argument when you don’t. In the case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where you want to localize the value of a string variable, use the string to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"create a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example shows how to create ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instances both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with and without localization. The title parameter provided to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Section","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a literal string, so SwiftUI creates a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedStringKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for it. However, the string entries in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageStore.today","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" array are ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" variables, so the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" views","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the list use the string values verbatim.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["List {","    Section(header: Text(\"Today\")) {","        ForEach(messageStore.today) { message in","            Text(message.title)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If the app is localized into Japanese with the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"translation of its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Localizable.strings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\"Today\" = \"今日\";"],"syntax":"other","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When run in Japanese, the example produces a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list like the following, localizing “Today” for the section header, but not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the list items."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI18LocalizedStringKeyV","title":"LocalizedStringKey","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LocalizedStringKey"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LocalizedStringKey"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LocalizedStringKey\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LocalizedStringKey\/init(stringInterpolation:)","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LocalizedStringKey\/init(stringLiteral:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentat